==English==

===Etymology===
''ig-'' (from ''[[ignorant]]'') + ''[[gnostic]]'' + ''-[[ism]]''. Coined by [[w:Rabbi Sherwin Wine|Rabbi Sherwin Wine]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# Belief that other beliefs regarding the existence or non-existence of deities all assume too much, especially because there is not just one universal definition of the word "God" (which therefore makes the word meaningless) or because the concept of "God" is [[unfalsifiable]] and [[unverifiable]]; also called "theological noncognitivism".

